kyler murray one of the big stories of  the day yesterday a couple of stories  kareem hunt calamari we're going to  start with kyler murray kyler murray is  now fully committed to playing football  so he says for now so someone says for  now and i'm going to be cynical here i  like colimer and i wish him the best but  i'm not doing my job if i don't take a  hard look at the things that are being  said and done to try to get to the  bottom of what's really happening and  i've been skeptical for a while now that  murray is going to try to play both  sides of this he's going to try to keep  a foot in each boat  as he pro progresses through february  march and april and makes a final  decision about whether to play football  after he sees who drafts him and how  high he's drafted but in order to get  drafted as high as possible you can't  say that you have to go all in with  football the statement that was posted  yesterday on his twitter page may or may  not have been written by him the a's  reportedly believe it was written by his  new agent eric burkhart the statement  reads as follows moving forward i am  firmly and fully committing my life and  time to becoming an nfl quarterback  football has been my love and passion my  entire life i was raised to play  quarterback and i very much look forward  to dedicating 100 of myself to being the  best possible quarterback and winning  nfl championships i have started an  extensive training program to further  prepare myself for upcoming nfl workouts  and interviews i eagerly await the  opportunity to continue to prove to nfl  decision makers that i am the franchise  quarterback in this draft okay  here's the thing  if he was raised to play quarterback if  football has been his love and passion  his entire life why did he take money  from the oakland a's last year when they  drafted them plenty of guys get drafted  they don't take the money from the team  why did he do it  why  that's the first question i'm asking in  indianapolis in two weeks at the  scouting combine  these interviews  for kyler murray  when you consider the circumstances when  you consider the fact that he did take  the money from the a's when you consider  the fact that the a's are still there  and i think the a's are playing this  beautifully we wrote about this last  night ken rosenthal of the athletic has  taken the view that the a's are still in  this the a's are ready to go the a's  aren't constrained by the same  limitations that will prevent what an  nfl team can pay  kyler murray that the a's can offer more  whatever the team that drafts kyle or  murray is able to pay under the cba the  a's can pay more and the a's seem to be  determined to still try to get kyler  murray now whether or not they really  are determined  and let's just take them at their word  that they are determined that throws a  hell of a wrench into the gears for kyle  murray because no matter what he says no  matter what he does  that pathway remains  back to baseball it's there he can go  back to baseball whenever he wants  because the a's are making it clear hey  we're fine well no we're not upset we  could be upset we could tell this kid i  forget it we're done with you we're not  playing this game we're not going to be  your leverage against the nfl we're  going to move on to someone else but  they're not  they are determined to still sign kyler  murray which is going to complicate  murray's life over the next two and a  half months because he's going to be  asked over and over and over again and  this time around when he is in these  15-minute meetings at the scouting  combine and when he's otherwise meeting  with teams he's not going to have  handlers there he's not going to have  agents here his dad's not going to be  there that awkward interview that he had  with dan patrick super bowl week  dan at one point said dad can can he  answer the question dad's a little  involved dad's not going to be involved  at the scouting combine kyle is going to  have to go in and he's going to have to  answer these questions and the teams are  going to be looking for reasons not to  take him especially because you're going  to have scouts in pretty much every team  that is arguing against kylie murray  because of his size not just his height  but his size we had russell wilson and  kyla murray at the set that we had at  radio row in atlanta just a couple of  hours apart and i i was struck  by how much smaller kyle murray is than  russell wilson they're both short but  wilson  wilson has that nfl quarterback  thickness to him where you can look at  him and say this guy can walk out there  between the white lines and protect  himself  murray  he just he looks little i'd be nervous  i'd be scared are you sure you're all  right out there kyler do you know what  you're doing these are really big strong  guys are you sure you can handle  yourself out there because you're not  really all that big and i don't know  that his frame allows him to pack on all  that much muscle i mean seven years ago  russell wilson wasn't built like he is  now i just don't know that murray's  frame is going to allow it there's a  picture floating around and i need to  post this at the website at some point  of murray standing with dwayne haskins  and tonga or tuatanga viloa of alabama  at the heisman  ceremonies  i i  it's it's it's jaw dropping how much  smaller murray is especially than  haskins and now haskins and murray are  the two quarterbacks in the draft pool  the two two of the names we're going to  hear the most about going into late  april so  and these are issues that he is not  going to be able to get away from and  he's going to be facing tough questions  tough scrutiny about  his size his stature and whether or not  he truly is committed to playing  football because look  whether whether he believes it at this  point or not  if he ends up going lower than he thinks  he should go and he said it himself in  this statement  he wants to prove that i am the  franchise quarterback in this draft  right so if he's the third quarterback  taken the second quarterback taken  anything other than the first name off  the board does that change his view on  the nfl well these teams have gotten it  wrong they're not properly assessing my  skills so i'm gonna maybe have second  thoughts about playing football maybe  i'll play baseball instead and if you've  got the a's there throwing more money on  the pile  yeah it's a heck of a risk there's a  risk that you're going to be the tampa  bay buccaneers in 1986 drafting bo  jackson first overall and he never plays  for you  because see football teams only hold  rights for one year  after a year kyle murray goes back into  the draft poll assuming someone drafts  him if no one drafts him then he's a  free agent able to sign with anyone at  any time  but  if he's drafted those rights last for  one year and then he goes back into the  draft pool next year remember 1986 1987  86 it was the bucks in round one  bo jackson didn't play football 87  the raiders took a seventh round flyer  at a time when there were 12 rounds in  the draft and bo jackson said yeah i'll  play football part-time and and i really  do think  that kyler murray's preference would be  if he could find a way to pull it off  and i think he's going to try to do it  although i don't think he is going to  get anywhere with it he'd like to play  both  he said that to us  he'd really like to play both he knows  it's highly highly highly highly  unlikely but he didn't say it's  impossible  i don't know that he can pull it off he  probably can't but if he's even holding  out hope of playing both then there is a  chance that this full commitment to  football isn't as full as he would say  and look we have to be cynical we have  to be skeptical we have to understand  that this this is part of the game it's  no different than running 40 yards in a  straight line or how high you can jump  or all the things you do at the scouting  combine there's a certain ritual to this  the things you do the things you say to  get drafted as high as possible the goal  between now and the end of april is to  get drafted as high as possible then  after you get drafted wherever you're  drafted you figure out what you're going  to do  just because you've been drafted doesn't  mean that you are legally committed to  playing for that team  the giants reportedly are out on  kyler murray they believe he's too small  i guess a team called the giants would  be  you know the most likely to have  concerns about size but look at that  look at this  look  there's another angle where it's even  more jaw dropping  but the difference between look at the  difference between haskins and murr they  play the same position  and haskins  has been spectacular  if i'm dwayne haskins i'm getting upset  by all this kyler murray talk hey people  you forget about me  passer and a runner not just a runner  some some would say just a runner no no  no no dwayne haskins pastor ander  and uh  look these size concerns are going to be  an issue maybe maybe maybe murray's  genius here is he's making the issue his  commitment to football and not his size  but here's reality it's going to be both  and you're going to have voices  in these organizations saying between  the risk that he's going to go play  baseball versus the reality that he  isn't as big as he should be it's not  worth it let's draft a guy that we know  is going to show up see murray is the  worst nightmare for an nfl team when  it's time to make a draft pick because  unlike every other guy that they may  draft murray has a very viable and  realistic option to play another  professional sport and make as much or  possibly more money  most guys  they don't have that  and the fact that you don't get that  commitment at the time you draft the guy  that you then have to sign him to a  contract that could be the thing that  scares  some teams away and we'll have plenty of  time to talk about  which teams may be seriously interested  in kyler murray and this whole draft  process he'll have the pro day workout  he'll have the scouting combine but that  those three days are already stressful  enough for the guys who go to  indianapolis with all the poking and the  prodding and the dehumanizing treatment  it's going to be even worse for kyle  murray because i think that anyone who  was paying attention to the dan patrick  interview from a couple of weeks ago  that they're going to be ready to  to really push this guy to see if he has  what it takes to be an nfl quarterback  from the standpoint of answering  questions in a confident manner carrying  himself a certain way  making it clear that he really is all in  with football that he can be trusted in  that regard and  uh  that he's not going to eventually have a  change of heart and oh by the way one  last point i mentioned that eric  burkhart is reportedly his agent  burkhardt also represents  cardinals coach cliff kingsbury who has  said that that and this was months ago  that if he had the first pick in the nfl  draft he would take kyler murray so that  isn't going away anytime soon even  though the cardinals have josh rosen  under contract they could end up having  rosen under contract and kyler murray's  draft rights and i do have a feeling  that if kyle murray were the first  overall pick in the draft he's probably  going to go ahead and sign an nfl  contract the question is how many picks  after number one  will it take for him to start thinking  maybe i need to change my mind about my  100 commitment to football  hi i'm mike tarico and thanks for  watching make sure to hit subscribe for  the latest news and highlights from nbc  sports

